# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for luneos-camera-tests.
#
# The Qt libraries in the sysroot are not built with -fsanitize=thread, so the
# synchronisation inside them is invisible to TSan: QMutex is a bare futex,
# and QThreadPool and the event queue hand work between threads under it.
# Anything handed over that way looks unsynchronised:
#
# - a queued call: BarcodeScanner's worker builds the call (the guard and the
#   decoded symbol) in QMetaObject::invokeMethod() and the GUI thread runs it
#   from QObject::event(); every access to it, and to the strings it carries,
#   is reported. invokeMethodCallableHelper(), where the worker builds it, is
#   in every one of those reports.
race:invokeMethodCallableHelper
#   ... and the event that carries it, deleted by the GUI thread once run.
race:QMetaObject::invokeMethodImpl
#
#   The decoded text itself: its QString data is allocated on the worker and
#   reference-counted on the GUI thread once the queued call runs.
race:QArrayData::allocate2
#
# - QThreadPool's own wait condition, destroyed on the GUI thread after its
#   worker has left it.
race:QWaitCondition
